hod is also appropriate for non-stationary objectives and problems with","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,286.24,455.42,295.94],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ea39dd9740c9782e5","kind":"glyph","char":"very noisy and/or sparse gradients. The hyper-parameters have intuitive interpre-","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,296.91,455.42,306.6],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"edebdde2ca8d3d271","kind":"glyph","char":"tations and typically require little tuning. Some connections to related algorithms,","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,307.57,455.42,317.27],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"efaf1f62c1870c687","kind":"glyph","char":"on which","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,318.24,175.81,327.93],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e481caa525dbbe956","kind":"glyph","char":"Adam","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal","bbox":[178.37,318.24,200.99,327.93],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"eddcaabbbfcbc67e4","kind":"glyph","char":"was inspired, are discussed. We also analyze the theoretical con-","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[203.54,318.24,455.42,327.93],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"eacd19d640d529d34","kind":"glyph","char":"vergence properties of the algorithm and provide a regret bound on the conver-","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,328.9,455.42,338.6],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e770fe10617ebe465","kind":"glyph","char":"gence rate that is comparable to the best known results under the online convex","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,339.56,455.42,349.26],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e1b5dc5abd2431c7d","kind":"glyph","char":"optimization framework. Empirical results demonstrate that Adam works well in","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,350.23,455.42,359.92],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e91c0ef1ed0412860","kind":"glyph","char":"practice and compares favorably to other stochastic optimization methods. Finally,","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,360.89,455.42,370.59],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ee338e01d2d25f508","kind":"glyph","char":"we discuss","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[139.86,371.56,181.6,381.25],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e4f143a8bf07b2ee2","kind":"glyph","char":"AdaMax","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal","bbox":[184.02,371.56,216.87,381.25],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ef45ede7303153458","kind":"glyph","char":", a variant of","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[216.87,371.56,265.62,381.25],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ead6424958bde3c64","kind":"glyph","char":"Adam","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal","bbox":[268.05,371.56,290.66,381.25],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e4fb4fc64d2b6329c","kind":"glyph","char":"based on the infinity norm.","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[293.09,371.56,397.31,381.25],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e68c03c66f900ce72","kind":"glyph","char":"1","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[105.25,404.47,111.07,416.1],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ec42d8f362357a0b3","kind":"glyph","char":"I","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[123.28,404.47,127.16,416.1],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ebee7ad2c98acbe9c","kind":"glyph","char":"NTRODUCTION","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[127.74,406.79,200.31,416.1],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"edbee218903f26afb","kind":"glyph","char":"Stochastic gradient-based optimization is of core practical importance in many fields of science and","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,423.1,490.32,432.8],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ed08becc15a611299","kind":"glyph","char":"engineering. Many problems in these fields can be cast as the optimization of some scalar parameter-","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,433.77,490.32,443.46],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e50072dd44cf86282","kind":"glyph","char":"ized objective function requiring maximization or minimization with respect to its parameters. If the","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,444.43,490.32,454.13],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e1c17ceac5754b253","kind":"glyph","char":"function is differentiable w.r.t. its parameters, gradient descent is a relatively efficient optimization","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,455.09,490.32,464.79],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e298ca4ea88734db7","kind":"glyph","char":"method, since the computation of first-order partial derivatives w.r.t. all the parameters is of the same","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,465.76,490.32,475.45],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e59dfe937b55d392a","kind":"glyph","char":"computational complexity as just evaluating the function. Often, objective functions are stochastic.","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,476.42,490.32,486.12],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e1a8adc1197dee33e","kind":"glyph","char":"For example, many objective functions are composed of a sum of subfunctions evaluated at different","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,487.09,490.32,496.78],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e8bf6acffecad2385","kind":"glyph","char":"subsamples of data; in this case optimization can be made more efficient by taking gradient steps","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,497.75,490.32,507.45],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e659e7f975f70065c","kind":"glyph","char":"w.r.t. individual subfunctions, i.e. stochastic gradient descent (SGD) or ascent. SGD proved itself","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,508.42,490.32,518.11],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"eb6e620bd5fafdf40","kind":"glyph","char":"as an efficient and effective optimization method that was central in many machine learning success","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,519.08,490.32,528.78],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"efd0214511ebadf01","kind":"glyph","char":"stories, such as recent advances in deep learning (Deng et al., 2013; Krizhevsky et al., 2012; Hinton","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,529.75,490.32,539.44],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e27a0aa0fbbcbad72","kind":"glyph","char":"& Salakhutdinov, 2006; Hinton et al., 2012a; Graves et al., 2013). Objectives may also have other","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,540.41,490.32,550.11],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e7aa500beb8a35779","kind":"glyph","char":"sources of noise than data subsampling, such as dropout (Hinton et al., 2012b) regularization. For","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,551.07,490.32,560.77],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e006e63702fcfde0a","kind":"glyph","char":"all such noisy objectives, efficient stochastic optimization techniques are required. The focus of this","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,561.74,490.32,571.43],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e8908a51f4b01eadc","kind":"glyph","char":"paper is on the optimization of stochastic objectives with high-dimensional parameters spaces. In","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,572.4,490.32,582.1],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ec30c7f8b7998e91d","kind":"glyph","char":"these cases, higher-order optimization methods are ill-suited, and discussion in this paper will be","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,583.07,490.32,592.76],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e4a3df827960dc07b","kind":"glyph","char":"restricted to first-order methods.","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,593.73,229.9,603.43],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e3bcda584a0f02db2","kind":"glyph","char":"We propose","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,610.21,151.11,619.91],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e564412cd5c385f29","kind":"glyph","char":"Adam","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal","bbox":[153.87,610.21,176.49,619.91],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e7cbc86d8b8f0d3af","kind":"glyph","char":", a method for efficient stochastic optimization that only requires first-order gra-","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[176.49,610.21,490.31,619.91],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ea0a5a667d5bae65a","kind":"glyph","char":"dients with little memory requirement. The method computes individual adaptive learning rates for","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,620.88,490.32,630.57],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e98b16ed9c8a61c94","kind":"glyph","char":"different parameters from estimates of first and second moments of the gradients; the name","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,631.54,464.76,641.24],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"eca02cabd60dbd308","kind":"glyph","char":"Adam","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal","bbox":[467.7,631.54,490.32,641.24],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e5c5f5a647c0b5725","kind":"glyph","char":"is derived from adaptive moment estimation. Our method is designed to combine the advantages","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,642.21,490.32,651.9],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"eeda17c1ec0004b5b","kind":"glyph","char":"of two recently popular methods: AdaGrad (Duchi et al., 2011), which works well with sparse gra-","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,652.87,490.32,662.57],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"ee3be16872be696b4","kind":"glyph","char":"dients, and RMSProp (Tieleman & Hinton, 2012), which works well in on-line and non-stationary","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,663.54,490.32,673.23],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"e69039a7e79d32b03","kind":"glyph","char":"settings; important connections to these and other stochastic optimization methods are clarified in","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,674.2,490.32,683.9],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidence":0.93,"rule":"body-font"},{"id":"edcb6b3a9999276b9","kind":"glyph","char":"section 5. Some of Adam’s advantages are that the magnitudes of parameter updates are invariant to","font":"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu","bbox":[104.96,684.87,490.32,694.56],"pathHash":"","ordinal":0,"label":"text","confidenc